Relative to an orthonormal basis ${vb(e_1), vb(e_2), vb(e_3)}$, writing $vb(a) = sum_i a_i vb(e_i)$ and $vb(b) = sum_j b_j vb(e_j)$ gives
$ vb(a) dot vb(b) = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3, quad abs(vb(a))^2 = a_1^2 + a_2^2 + a_3^2. $
In $RR^n$ this coordinate formula defines the dot product directly, $vb(a) dot vb(b) = sum_(i=1)^n a_i b_i$, and it satisfies $vb(e_i) dot vb(e_j) = delta_(i j)$.
